\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now I have found the ground wherein
\par Sure my soul's anchor may remain-
\par The wounds of Jesus, for my sin
\par Before the world's foundation slain;
\par Whose mercy shall unshaken stay,
\par When heaven and earth are fled away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Father, Thine everlasting grace
\par Our scanty thought surpasses far,
\par Thy heart still melts with tenderness,
\par Thy arms of love still open are
\par Returning sinners to receive,
\par That mercy they may taste and live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Love, Thou bottomless abyss,
\par My sins are swallowed up in Thee!
\par Covered is my unrighteousness,
\par Nor spot of guilty remains on me,
\par While Jesu's blood through earth 
\par and skies
\par Mercy, free, boundless mercy! cries.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With faith I plunge me in this sea,
\par Here is my hope, my joy, my rest;
\par Hither, when hell assails, I flee,
\par I look into my Saviour's breast:
\par Away, sad doubt and anxious fear!
\par Mercy is all that's written there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Though waves and storms go o'er 
\par my head,
\par Though strength, and health, and
\par friends be gone,
\par Though joys be withered all and dead,
\par Though every comfort be withdrawn,
\par On this my steadfast soul relies-
\par Father, Thy mercy never dies!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Fixed on this ground will I remain,
\par Though my heart fail and fresh decay;
\par This anchor shall my soul sustain,
\par When earth's foundation melt away:
\par Mercy's full power I then shall prove,
\par Loved with an everlasting love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

